From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Alexander M. Merritt" <alexander@edera.dev>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:16:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] configs/devices: add the devices that Edera's Xen boot tests
 use

Xen's CI boots Xen on the virt machine with only a few devices
beside those the machine selects. A build of just those devices is
short enough to run in the CI job that boots it, so the job needs no
prebuilt QEMU.

Signed-off-by: Alexander M. Merritt <alexander@edera.dev>
---
 configs/devices/aarch64-softmmu/xen-boot.mak | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 configs/devices/aarch64-softmmu/xen-boot.mak

diff --git a/configs/devices/aarch64-softmmu/xen-boot.mak b/configs/devices/aarch64-softmmu/xen-boot.mak
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..3f5a76ab4c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/configs/devices/aarch64-softmmu/xen-boot.mak
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+# The devices that Edera's Xen boot tests use, beside those the virt machine
+# selects itself. Configure with:
+#
+#   --without-default-devices --with-devices-aarch64=xen-boot
+
+CONFIG_ARM_VIRT=y
+
+# The ESP that the firmware boots Xen from.
+CONFIG_VIRTIO_PCI=y
+CONFIG_VIRTIO_BLK=y
+
+# A console UART behind a PCI Express port, as on Graviton.
+CONFIG_PCIE_PORT=y
+CONFIG_SERIAL_PCI=y
